From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:39:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Add a forced integer draw to the C ABI

hegel_generate_integer_forced records a caller-chosen value as an ordinary
integer choice in the given bounds, consuming the choice position without
consulting the choice sequence or the RNG and marking the node forced, as
the forced boolean of hegel_generate_boolean already does. A frontend whose
own code decides a value at a choice position (Hypothesis's filtered
sampled_from, and its constant injection) needs this so its sequence stays
aligned with libhegel's, replays through blobs, and shrinks as recorded.
Backed by a new `generate_integer_forced` on the backend trait over the
existing NativeTestCase::draw_integer_forced; validated like the other
integer draws, and spanned the same way. Pins the seed of the NaN-with-
bounds ABI test, whose NaN share is a per-case drawn parameter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
